# Per-user runtime settings. tiko rewrites these as you use it, so tracking them means
# every run shows up as a diff and every pull risks a conflict over someone else's window
# positions and key bindings.
#
# Paths are anchored with a leading "/" on purpose: settings/keywords/*.ini ARE tracked
# (codetips.ini and friends), so a bare *.ini rule would wrongly catch those too.
/settings/keybindings.ini
/settings/settings.ini

# Internal design / planning notes. NEVER published: this repo is public on GitHub
# and clients can browse it.
REFACTOR_PLAN*.md

# Env-gated theme diagnostics (TIKO_THEME_TRACE=1), and the self-test's scratch file.
/theme_dump.txt
/theme_trace.log
/_theme_selftest.tmp

# The Help Center's WebView2 profile: cache, cookies and local storage, created by the
# runtime on first open. Machine-specific and regenerated on demand -- never committed.
# (WebView2Loader.dll IS committed; it is a shipped binary, like bin\Scintilla64.dll.)
/settings/webview2/

# The generated Help Center site: ~31,700 files / ~147 MB, and every helpgen regeneration
# rewrites all of them (the page shell carries cache-busting ?v= hashes), so tracking it
# would add ~31k blobs to history per regen -- permanently, since removing them later means
# a filter-repo force-push that breaks every clone. Staged from C:\dev\HelpCenter\site by
# _copy_helpcenter.bat instead. WITHOUT IT THE HELP CENTER REPORTS ITS FILES AS MISSING,
# so a fresh clone needs that script run once.
/settings/helpcenter/
